   'Share of organizations using physical AI at least minimally, by region, today and expected in two years', 'Director-level to C-suite leaders surveyed August-September 2025, split by Americas, EMEA and Asia Pacific', '% of surveyed companies',
   '%', 0, 'category',
   'Self-reported by executives (N=3,235 overall); ''at least minimal use'' is a low bar that a single pilot robot would clear, so this is not a measure of robotics intensity. The ''in 2 years'' series is a stated expectation, i.e. a projection. Regional bases as printed in the report are ''Americas N=3,235, EMEA N=1,170, AP N=475'' - the Americas figure is the full-sample N and appears to be a labelling error in the source, so treat the Americas base as uncertain and the AP base (475) as small.', 'p. 23', 'Figure 10: Extent of physical AI usage (percent) ... Question: To what extent is your organization currently utilizing physical AI (e.g., robotics, automated machinery) in its operations?',
