   'AI benefits organizations say they are achieving today versus benefits they hope to achieve', '3,235 director-level to C-suite leaders across six industries and 24 countries, surveyed August-September 2025', '% of surveyed companies',
   '%', 0, 'category',
   'Executives grading their own organizations (N=3,235); ''achieving today'' is a claim, not a measured gain - no revenue, cost or productivity figure is attached to any of it. Multiple-select, so shares do not sum to 100. The two series are answers to two different questions, so a benefit can score lower on ''hope to achieve'' simply because respondents already counted it as achieved. An ''Other'' category (1% on both series) is omitted here.', 'p. 10', 'Figure 2: AI benefits achieving today vs. hope to achieve (percent) ... Question: With regards to benefits from your AI efforts: Which benefits are you achieving today? Which benefits do you hope to achieve?',
