   '%', 0, 'category',
   'This is executives grading their own organization''s readiness (N=3,235) - a self-assessment with no external benchmark, and the report itself notes strategy and governance scores rise fastest because they ''depend primarily on executive decision-making and policy development'' rather than on anything being built. Only the ''highly prepared'' share of each four-point scale is shown here; the remaining shares (moderately, slightly, not prepared) are omitted. Deloitte reports year-on-year changes of +4pp technology infrastructure, +3pp strategy, +3pp data management, +6pp risk and governance and +2pp talent, but the arrows accompanying the falls described in the text are not unambiguous in the source, so no change figures are charted here.', 'p. 28', 'Figure 12: Level of preparedness for AI adoption (percent) ... Question: For each, rate your organization''s level of preparedness with respect to broadly adopting AI tools/applications.',
   11)
