   'Job postings requiring AI skills, by country', 'AI-skill postings as a share of all job postings tracked in each country, 2025', '% of all job postings',
   '%', 2, 'category',
   'Underlying data is Lightcast''s job-postings database, not an official labour statistic. It measures advertised demand, not hires or filled roles, and coverage of online postings varies by country — a small labour market with a heavily online job board will look more AI-intensive than one where hiring happens off-platform. The report also warns that historical posting counts get revised. Eleven countries shown here; the full series is split across two charts.', 'p. 34 (report p. 204)', 'In 2025, Singapore led with 4.69% of all job postings that required AI skills, followed by Hong Kong (3.5%), Luxembourg (3.4%), and Spain (3.3%). The United States reached 2.6%, followed by Chile (2.4%) and the United Kingdom (1.9%).',
