   'Phase of the AI journey organizations place themselves in', 'Senior leaders at organizations with US$50m+ revenue across 20 countries and territories, Q1 2026 (n=2,110) against Q2 2026 (n=2,145)', '% of organizations',
   '%', 0, 'category',
   'A quarterly executive survey: 2,145 senior leaders self-selecting a phase for their own organization, fielded online 28 April to 25 May 2026. Self-placement on a six-point maturity ladder is a judgement, not an audited measure — a leader claiming ''driving adoption'' is not evidence AI is embedded at scale. The Q1 and Q2 waves are separate samples of respondents, not the same organizations tracked over time, so quarter-on-quarter shifts partly reflect sample composition. Percentages are rounded and sum to 100 within rounding.', 'p. 10', 'The largest movement this quarter occurred in the driving-adoption phase ... Which of the following best describes the phase your organization is in its AI journey? Q1 (n=2110), Q2 (n=2145)',
