   'Share of organizations using AI, and gen AI, in at least one business function', 'Respondents to McKinsey''s Global Survey on the state of AI, 2017 to 2025; the latest point comes from 1,491 participants in 101 nations surveyed 16-31 July 2024', '% of respondents',
   '%', 0, 'year',
   'Survey self-report, not an administrative count: a respondent saying their organization has ''adopted'' AI in one function can mean anything from a few employees experimenting to embedded redesigned processes - McKinsey states it deliberately left ''adopted'' undefined. The definition of AI use also changed twice (in 2017 it meant AI in a core part of the business or at scale; 2018-19 meant embedding at least one AI capability; since 2020 it means adoption in at least one function), so the early points are not comparable with the later ones. The x-axis is labelled by publication year, so the ''2025'' point is the survey fielded 16-31 July 2024. Data are weighted by each respondent''s nation''s contribution to global GDP. The gen AI series begins in 2023.', 'p. 16', 'Organizations'' use of AI has accelerated markedly in the past year, after years of little meaningful change. Organizations that use AI in at least 1 business function, % of respondents',
   12)
