VALUES
  ('mckinsey-gen-ai-cost-decrease-by-function', 'productivity', NULL,
   'McKinsey & Company (QuantumBlack)', 'The State of AI: How Organizations Are Rewiring to Capture Value', 'https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/the-state-of-ai-how-organizations-are-rewiring-to-capture-value', '2025-03-01',
   'Share of respondents reporting a cost decrease in the business unit using gen AI, by function', 'Respondents whose organizations use gen AI in the given function; first-half 2024 survey (fielded 22 Feb - 5 Mar 2024) compared with second-half 2024 survey (16-31 July 2024)', '% of respondents',
   '%', 0, 'category',
   'Self-reported perception of cost change within a business unit, not audited cost data, and not net of what gen AI itself cost to build and run. Values are the totals printed at the end of each stacked bar, summing three bands; segments may not sum exactly to the printed total because of rounding. The band definitions differ slightly between the two waves (first half: 20% or more / 10-19% / under 10%; second half: 20% or more / 11-19% / 10% or less), so the two series are not perfectly like-for-like. Asked only of those reporting gen AI use in that function; ''cost increase'', ''no change'', ''not applicable'' and ''don''t know'' are excluded, and manufacturing is omitted because the base was too small to report.', 'p. 23', 'Respondents increasingly report cost reductions from gen AI within business units using the technology. Cost decrease within business units from gen AI use, past 12 months, by function, % of respondents',
