VALUES
  ('oecd-median-labour-productivity-growth', 'productivity', NULL,
   'OECD', 'OECD Economic Outlook, Volume 2026 Issue 1', 'https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/2026/06/oecd-economic-outlook-volume-2026-issue-1_8be0dba6.html', '2026-06-01',
   'Median labour productivity growth across OECD economies', 'Output per person employed, median of OECD economies, first half of 2024 versus fourth quarter of 2025', '% growth in output per person employed',
   '%', 1, 'year',
   'A cyclical recovery, not an established trend: the OECD notes the 1.2% rate is only back in line with the 2010-19 average, and it attributes the pickup to a recovery in productivity growth broadly rather than to AI. Only in the United States country note does the OECD link stronger productivity growth to AI, and there only as ''likely driven by the capital deepening linked to AI-related investment''. Output per person employed does not adjust for hours worked, and a median across economies hides wide country variation.', 'p. 25', 'Median labour productivity growth (output per person employed) across OECD economies rose from 0.3% in the first half of 2024 to 1.2% by the fourth quarter of 2025, a rate that was broadly in line with the average pace through 2010-19.',
