VALUES
  ('pwc-ai-skill-wage-premium-by-sector', NULL, 'labour',
   'PwC', '2026 Global AI Jobs Barometer', 'https://www.pwc.com/gx/en/issues/artificial-intelligence/job-barometer/2026/2026-global-ai-jobs-barometer-full-report.pdf', NULL,
   'Wage premium for workers with AI skills, by sector', 'Advertised salaries in online job postings, 2025, eight PwC-aligned sectors, global', '% higher advertised salary vs comparable non-AI roles',
   '%', 0, 'category',
   'A snapshot of one year, not a growth rate. Premiums are the gap between advertised salaries for roles requiring AI skills and comparable roles that do not, within the same sector — so they reflect what employers advertise, not what workers are paid, and they do not control for firm size, seniority or location beyond the sector split. Only eight of the sixteen sectors in PwC''s scope are shown; the 62% average is calculated across all sixteen.', 'p. 23', 'Wage premiums for workers with AI skills have risen to 62% (from 57% in last year’s Barometer’) Wage premium by sector, (%, 2025)',
