VALUES
  ('pwc-headcount-growth-by-ai-exposure', 'jobs', NULL,
   'PwC', '2026 Global AI Jobs Barometer', 'https://www.pwc.com/gx/en/issues/artificial-intelligence/job-barometer/2026/2026-global-ai-jobs-barometer-full-report.pdf', NULL,
   'Firm headcount growth since 2018, most vs least AI-exposed companies', 'Average firm growth in employee numbers against a 2018 baseline, 2022-2025, companies with turnover of at least $50m USD, global', '% growth in headcount vs 2018',
   '%', 1, 'year',
   'PwC states explicitly that this ORBIS company data is not intended to represent economy-wide employment growth. Only larger formal firms with financial and headcount data in both 2018 and 2024/25 are included; firms that exited during the period are dropped, creating survivorship bias, and reporting requirements vary by country. Exposure is a sector-level proxy, not observed AI use. The interpretable result is the gap between the quartiles, not the absolute growth rates.', 'p. 20', 'Perhaps surprisingly, headcount growth at the most AI-exposed companies is outpacing that at the least AI-exposed companies. Average firm growth rate in headcount by AI exposure quartile (measured using a 2018 baseline)',
