   'How human-intensive the new tasks added to jobs are, by AI exposure quartile', 'Average EPOCH score of newly added tasks per occupation, 2022-2025, all occupations grouped into AI exposure quartiles, global', 'Average EPOCH score (0-1) of new tasks',
   '', 2, 'category',
   'EPOCH is an index built by Loaiza and Rigobon (MIT) that scores how far a task relies on empathy, presence, opinion, creativity and hope. It is a constructed score on an arbitrary scale, not a count of anything observed — the ranking between quartiles is the signal, the absolute values are not units of anything. Tasks are inferred from the wording of job advertisements, so this measures what employers write down, not what workers do.', 'p. 16', 'New tasks added to AI-exposed roles since 2022 are 2.5x more likely to rely on ‘human-intensive’ capabilities such as empathy, creativity, and face to face presence. Average EPOCH score per occupation (new tasks only), by AI exposure quartile, 2022-2025',
