VALUES
  ('pwc-professionalised-vs-democratised-growth', 'entry-level', NULL,
   'PwC', '2026 Global AI Jobs Barometer', 'https://www.pwc.com/gx/en/issues/artificial-intelligence/job-barometer/2026/2026-global-ai-jobs-barometer-full-report.pdf', NULL,
   'Job postings and advertised salary growth, professionalised vs democratised jobs', 'Cumulative growth to 2025 in online job postings (from 2018) and average advertised salary (from 2021), six countries with Lightcast data back to 2012', '% cumulative growth to 2025',
   '%', 0, 'category',
   'The two series use different baselines — postings are indexed to 2018 and salaries to 2021 — so the bars are comparable within a series but not across them. Everything here is measured from online job advertisements, which describe vacancies rather than filled jobs or actual pay, and cover only six countries with data back to 2012. ''Professionalised'' and ''democratised'' are PwC''s classification of occupations using expertise scores from Teeselink and Carey (2026), mapped from US SOC-2018 codes onto international ISCO-08 codes to make global figures possible.', 'p. 8', 'professionalised salaries have grown 37% since 2021 and democratised by 26% - a 42% gap.',
