VALUES
  ('wef-jobs-created-vs-displaced-by-2030', NULL, 'labour',
   'World Economic Forum', 'Four Futures for Jobs in the New Economy: AI and Talent in 2030', 'https://www.weforum.org/publications/four-futures-for-jobs-in-the-new-economy-ai-and-talent-in-2030/', '2026-01-01',
   'Jobs projected to be created and displaced by 2030', 'Global macrotrend projection to 2030, drawn from the Forum''s Future of Jobs Report 2025', 'million jobs by 2030',
   'm', 0, 'category',
   'A projection, not a count of anything that has happened. It is attributed to all global macrotrends together — geoeconomic fragmentation, the green transition and demographics as well as technology — so it is not an estimate of AI''s effect alone. The report itself describes the figures as ''around'' and ''about''. The two numbers are gross flows, not the same jobs moving; the implied net is the report''s own framing, not a measured outcome.', 'p. 5', 'Global macrotrends – such as geoeconomic fragmentation, technological change, the green transition and others – are projected to create around 170 million new jobs by 2030, while displacing about 92 million existing jobs.',
   20)
